  "things": [
   {
    "id": "hearth_house",
    "at": [
     260,
     400
    ],
    "r": 55,
    "lines": [
     "* The hearth-house of Emberfold. They say its fire has never been let go out, in all the years the village has lived here.",
     "* The bread is baked on the bare rock of the hearth. Nobody asks travellers where they came from."
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "carved_lintel",
    "at": [
     385,
     398
    ],
    "r": 45,
    "lines": [
     "* Eight flames are cut in a row over the hearth-house door. One is cut deeper than the others, and its groove is black with old soot.",
     "* The other seven have worn almost smooth."
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "caldera_view",
    "at": [
     975,
     580
    ],
    "r": 55,
    "lines": [
     "* The caldera drops away in rings, each one hotter than the last. Far down, a red light swells and fades, slow as breathing.",
     "* Ten rings down to the heart, the villagers say. They live in the first two."
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "cistern",
    "at": [
     255,
     445
    ],
    "r": 50,
    "lines": [
     "* Water comes down to the village through a clay pipe from somewhere above, one drop at a time.",
     "* A chalk line on the stone marks today's share. Nobody has taken more than their line."
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "red_lanterns",
    "at": [
     520,
     515
    ],
    "r": 40,
    "lines": [
     "* The lanterns are red glass over plain oil flames.",
     "* Aud's people light them from the hearth every evening, one by one, and trim them by hand."
    ]
   }
  ],
